#====================================================================
# E2152 - Dangling symlink cleanup in Python package recipes
#====================================================================

id:                     E395
trigger_tool:           conan|python|package
phase:                  package
error_signature:        dangling symbolic link remains after target removal|broken symlink survives package cleanup|Path.is_file returns false for dangling symlink

severity:               2
category:               python, conan, symlink, package-integrity
match_keywords:         dangling symlink, broken symlink, Path.is_file, Path.is_symlink, unlink, package cleanup, metadata alias, conanmanifest
title:                  Remove dangling package aliases with explicit symlink detection

root_cause:             Python Path.is_file() follows a symbolic link and returns false after its target has been removed. Cleanup code guarded only by is_file() therefore skips a dangling alias even though the directory entry remains and may still be recorded in the package manifest.
affected_scope:         Python and Conan package finalizers that remove generated metadata files and their aliases, especially when a real target is removed before an alias symlink is inspected.
verification_cmd:       Reproduce a real file plus alias symlink, delete the target, run the cleanup, then require both lexists-style absence and a package consumer that rejects any file or symlink residue.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           explicit-file-or-symlink-unlink
rec_description:        For each prohibited package path, unlink it when Path.is_file() or Path.is_symlink() is true. Keep the path list explicit, then validate both normal files and deliberately dangling aliases with a negative package-integrity test.
rec_command:            |
  path = Path(package_folder, "lib", "obsolete-alias")
  if path.is_file() or path.is_symlink():
      path.unlink()
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-package-finalizer

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      lexists-lstat-classification
fallback_description:   Use os.path.lexists() or lstat() when the cleanup also needs to classify non-file residue, but still reject directories and unknown file types rather than recursively deleting them.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       if .*\.is_file\(\).*unlink
forbid_1_reason:        is_file() is false for a symbolic link whose target no longer exists.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package retains a broken alias and can publish an internally inconsistent manifest.

forbid_2_pattern:       rmtree|recursive.*delete|Remove-Item.*-Recurse
forbid_2_reason:        Broad recursive cleanup can erase unknown or foreign package content instead of proving the expected entry type.
forbid_2_consequence:   Package corruption or hidden upstream layout drift.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

